// The CONTRACT page: the request and response payloads {{.Source}} described,
// and one handler per operation. Domain entities live in types.go; payloads
// live here, because they ARE the contract.
//
// Every handler is a 501 stub: `api.Fail(501, <pkg>.<op>.not_implemented, ...)`
// rides the problem envelope, so a caller of an unported endpoint gets a real,
// machine-readable answer instead of a 404 or a panic. Porting one is a
// three-line edit — take the dependency on the receiver (or a closure), do the
// work, return the typed value — and the code const in errors.go goes with it.
